  "name": "Remove backgrounds from new WooCommerce product images with LassoCut",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6c75b809-639b-5acb-9e22-67e95f3d3502",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -800,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Remove backgrounds from new WooCommerce product images with LassoCut\n\n### Who it's for\nWooCommerce store owners who want every product photo on a clean white background for their shop, Google Shopping, Amazon or eBay, without editing images by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every hour** (or **Run now**) reads your **Settings**.\n2. **Get all products** lists the catalogue. Products that already carry the `lassocut_processed` marker or have no image are skipped, and each run is capped (20 products by default).\n3. For each product, the main image is downloaded, **LassoCut** removes the background and puts the product on white (JPG).\n4. The new image is uploaded to the **media library** and becomes the main product image. The original stays in the gallery and in the library, and the product gets the marker so it is never processed (or billed) twice.\n5. A failed product (broken image, no credits left...) is recorded and the loop moves on. **Build run summary** counts processed products, failures and credits used.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified community node **n8n-nodes-lassocut** (Settings > Community nodes).\n2. Create a free account at https://www.lassocut.com and add your API key as a **LassoCut API** credential.\n3. WooCommerce > Settings > Advanced > REST API: create a **Read/Write** key and add it as a **WooCommerce API** credential (used by **Get all products** and **Set as main product image**).\n4. Users > Profile > Application Passwords: create one and add it as a **Wordpress API** credential (username + application password) on **Upload to media library**.\n5. Put your store URL in **Settings**. Your store must use **https** (WooCommerce keys are refused over plain http).\n6. Test with **Run now**, then publish the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- WooCommerce 5+ on https, and a LassoCut account. Free accounts get 50 previews a month (up to 10 a day). A full-size result costs 1 credit. Credit packs start at $9 for 100 credits, and credits never expire.\n\n### How to customise\n- **Settings**: background colour (`ffffff`, `f5f5f5`...), size (`preview` is free for tests), format, marker name, products per run, keep the original in the gallery or not.\n- Replace the schedule with a **WooCommerce Trigger** (product.created) if n8n has a public URL.\n- Send the summary to Slack or email after **Build run summary**.\n- To redo a product, delete its `lassocut_processed` custom field.\n\n### Disclosure\nBuilt by the founder of LassoCut, who maintains the n8n-nodes-lassocut node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
